cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research artifact, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Privacy Lens: evidence-bounded permission-activity review for Android privacy assessment"
abstract: >-
  Privacy Lens is an offline, evidence-first Android research prototype that turns
  heterogeneous permission and activity evidence into review prompts while
  refusing to convert admission state into a legal conclusion. This repository is
  the reproducible publication artifact for the accompanying thesis; it contains
  the implementation, the verification pipeline, the canonical experiment
  configuration, the pinned evidence receipts, and the LaTeX thesis source.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Zhang"
    given-names: "Zhiheng"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zhiheng-zhang-Mera/privacy-lens-research-artifact"
license: LicenseRef-AllRightsReserved
keywords:
  - Android
  - privacy
  - GDPR
  - reproducible research
  - static analysis
  - evidence traceability
# Unreleased metadata. These fields are intentionally omitted rather than guessed:
#   doi:            no archival DOI has been minted for this artifact
#   version:        the version below tracks the prototype release, not a publication
#   date-released:  no public release date has been set
version: "1.15.0"
notes: >-
  The thesis document that this artifact accompanies is included as LaTeX source
  under Thesis/Final and as a compiled PDF under output/pdf. Publication status,
  venue, and DOI are unresolved and are not asserted here.
